WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.669 --> 00:00:03.111
- [Woman] In East London,
there is a building.

00:00:03.111 --> 00:00:05.013
It's known as the Cathedral on the Marsh,

00:00:05.013 --> 00:00:07.365
but this is no house of worship.

00:00:07.365 --> 00:00:10.061
It's a monument to London's sewers.

00:00:10.061 --> 00:00:12.894
(inspiring music)

00:00:13.881 --> 00:00:17.025
Opened in 1865, the
Crossness Pumping Station

00:00:17.025 --> 00:00:19.543
was one of the first of
its kind in the world.

00:00:19.543 --> 00:00:22.864
Designed in the Romanesque
style, the Victorian masterpiece

00:00:22.864 --> 00:00:25.636
was built to tackle London's
struggles with raw sewage

00:00:25.636 --> 00:00:28.917
and cholera outbreaks, which
killed up to 20,000 people

00:00:28.917 --> 00:00:30.332
every year.

00:00:30.332 --> 00:00:34.112
The plant is a testament to
beauty in both form and function

00:00:34.112 --> 00:00:38.279
Almost every inch is adorned
with immaculate ironwork.

00:00:38.461 --> 00:00:40.362
Long pillars support the top floor

00:00:40.362 --> 00:00:42.997
where four steam-powered
beam engines rest,

00:00:42.997 --> 00:00:44.830
weighing 47 tons each.

00:00:46.118 --> 00:00:47.952
The station was part of a system devised

00:00:47.952 --> 00:00:50.713
to collect sewage water and
discard it in the eastern part

00:00:50.713 --> 00:00:53.608
of the city away from the center.

00:00:53.608 --> 00:00:56.059
Despite there being other
regulations to reduce sewage

00:00:56.059 --> 00:00:58.995
at the time, the station
has been praised for pushing

00:00:58.995 --> 00:01:02.762
London into a healthier,
less smelly future.

00:01:02.762 --> 00:01:04.855
As the English capital
has moved to new solutions

00:01:04.855 --> 00:01:08.179
to keep its water clean and
flowing, this sewage cathedral

00:01:08.179 --> 00:01:10.581
is maintained as a
museum, showing that even

00:01:10.581 --> 00:01:13.642
the dirtiest of jobs can inspire beauty.

00:01:13.642 --> 00:01:16.475
(inspiring music)

00:01:20.128 --> 00:01:23.045
(piano note rings)

